<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Wesco yr share rises, div up.</title>
<headline>Wesco yr share rises, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)	  1,466    vs	930</p>
<p>    Shr, excl excepts (cts)  1,165    vs    1,054</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			135    vs	120</p>
<p>    Attrib income	     123.21    vs    78.14</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     323.70    vs   300.33</p>
<p>    Tax			   115.70    vs   133.93</p>
<p>    Interest paid		82.54    vs    84.63</p>
<p>    Turnover		  6,349.61    vs 6,180.67</p>
<p>    Share of associates'     10.98    vs    12.58</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  25.32    vs    10.40 loss</p>
<p>Full name: Wesco Investment Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it hoped for real growth in earnings from its major investments -- Toyota and Metair -- in the year ahead.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
